oxymesh — MeshCore-compatible firmware, written in Rust.

This project reimplements MeshCore's protocols (over-the-air packet format and companion
protocol) from a reading of its sources. No MeshCore file is copied. A few pieces of behaviour
are ported from it, each with its origin cited in the source:
  - the three notification tunes (RTTTL strings, examples/companion_radio/ui-new/UITask.cpp)
    in crates/mc-ui/src/tune.rs;
  - the noise-floor sampler (src/helpers/radiolib/RadioLibWrappers.cpp) in
    crates/mc-core/src/noise.rs;
  - the GPS handling (MicroNMEALocationProvider, EnvironmentSensorManager) in
    firmware/esp32s3/src/gps.rs and crates/mc-nmea;
  - the layout of the C++ firmware's files (examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp) read by
    crates/mc-spiffs.

